          ":question/worked-solution": "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{- 8 x + 3 y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x^{2}\\left(\\frac{- 8 x + 3 y}{x}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x (- 8 x + 3 y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 8 x^{2} + 3 x y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(- 3 x)}_{P(x)}y=\\underbrace{- 8 x^{2}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} - 3 x y=- 8 x^{2}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=- 3 x$ and $Q(x)=- 8 x^{2}.$",
